  "body_human_readable": "### Tesla's 2024 Sales Mark First Annual Decline in Over a Decade\n\nTesla sold approximately 1.79 million vehicles globally in 2024, a slight decrease of about 1.1% from the previous year's 1.81 million units. This marks the first time in twelve years that the electric vehicle manufacturer has experienced an annual drop in sales.\n\nDespite a stronger fourth quarter, with 495,570 vehicles delivered, the final push was not enough to overcome a slower start to the year. The fourth-quarter sales showed a 2.3% increase, aided by incentives like 0% financing and free charging.\n\nThe vast majority of sales in the last quarter of 2024 came from the Model 3 and Model Y, with only 23,640 of the higher-priced Model S, Model X, and the new Cybertruck being sold. For the entire year, the Model Y was the most popular, with 1.22 million units sold, followed by the Model 3 with 476,626 units.\n\nIn terms of production, Tesla manufactured 1.77 million vehicles in 2024, which was slightly less than its total deliveries. The company's global electric vehicle market share for 2024 stood at approximately 10.52%. This sales performance meant that for the first time, Tesla sold more cars than the German luxury brand Audi.\n\nAnalysts attribute the slowing sales growth to an aging model lineup and increased competition in major markets like China, Europe, and the United States. While Tesla used to dominate the EV market, there are now significantly more electric vehicle models available to consumers.",
